# Fork commits that carry each patch in patches/PsyCross/PATCHES.
#
# The submodule tracks a fork (see ORIGIN.txt) whose history already contains
# every patch here. Later fork commits edited the same regions, so six of the
# patches (0001, 0003, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010) no longer reverse-apply against
# the fork tip even though their changes are present: the surrounding context
# has drifted. Textual apply/reverse checks alone therefore cannot distinguish
# "present but drifted" from "missing", so each patch records the fork commit
# that introduced it and tools/apply_third_party_patches.sh treats a patch as
# satisfied when that commit is an ancestor of the submodule HEAD.
#
# A patch with no entry here, or whose commit is not an ancestor of the pin,
# falls back to `git apply`.
#
# Format: <patch file name> <commit sha in third_party/PsyCross>

